WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:05.270
Run!

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:07.570
There's something in the urinary tract!

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:12.190
The urine...

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:15.780
is bright red with blood.

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:20.870
I've never seen anything this massive.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.160
What should we do?

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:24.580
There's nothing...

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:27.040
that we can do!

00:02:03.970 --> 00:02:05.980
EPISODE 6:
KIDNEYS, KIDNEY STONES, AND TEARS

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:08.730
Yo! Good work!

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.230
Where are you heading back from?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.400
The small intestine.
They just yelled at me to bring more oxygen.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.440
Seems like nobody has enough.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.530
Oh well, let's do our part
and deliver as much as we can.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.950
What's going on here?

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.080
The waste is all backed up
because of dehydration.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.040
We're seeing more and more
of these blood vessels lately, huh—

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:36.380
Whoa! Whoa! Whoa!

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.550
Are you okay?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:47.430
I could've fallen!
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:49.600
Well, I don't want to be
the only one getting dirty!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.900
Stay away from me! Whoa!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.530
Oh man! Come on!
Stop fooling around!

00:02:57.820 --> 00:02:59.240
Your face is a mess.

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:01.820
So is yours.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.830
Jeez, thanks to you, I'm sticky all over.
It feels disgusting!

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.290
My bad!

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:16.590
But the kidneys
aren't too far from here, right?

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.420
Let's go get cleaned up.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.260
Hey, good idea!

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.930
NEPHRON

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:25.930
This is it!

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:32.730
The liver's a fun place, too, but the Glomeruli here
have a kind of grace. That's what I like about it!

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:39.570
TALKING IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.900
Thanks for looking after me today, Glomerulus.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.150
<i>The Glomeruli.</i>

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.740
<i>Their job is to filter the blood.</i>

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:51.500
Hello there! Here I am again!
Take good care of me today, okay?

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.460
How have you been?
I'm grungier than usual today, huh?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.210
I suppose so.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:00.920
Yeah, but wouldn't you say
that's the measure of a working man?

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.880
Thank you so much
for all your hard work.

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:03.930
Hey, you there!

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.890
You need to move your hands,
not your mouth!

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:13.560
TALKING IS STRICTLY FORBIDDEN

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.730
Uh, sorry about that.

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.020
<i>The kidneys.</i>

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:20.150
<i>Organs made up of approximately
one million nephrons,</i>

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:24.070
<i>each of which are comprised
of renal tubules attached to Glomeruli...</i>

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.780
<i>which filter the blood.</i>

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.040
<i>Urine is the by-product
of this filtering process.</i>

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:37.250
Hey, hey! I'm still not clean!
Do a better job of washing it off!

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:38.710
I'm so sorry.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.920
For heaven's sake, we're the ones
running around all day, and we're exhausted!

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:47.600
Unlike you people who do nothing
but stand around like statues!

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.010
That's no way to talk.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:51.640
We're used to it.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:53.600
It's fine.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:01.030
Well, I appreciate it.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.990
All that you Glomeruli do for us...

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.530
24/7, 365 days a year...

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.450
you keep filtering the blood for us.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:16.080
It's thanks to you that we can
deliver oxygen in a clean state.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:23.670
Not to mention, the blood's been all gooey lately,
so I'm sure you've been busy.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:27.550
Overeating... Overdrinking...

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:31.350
This body's blood vessels are so clogged up,

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:34.270
it's only a matter of time
before something happens.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.730
On top of that,
there's been a rise in oxalic acid lately...

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.980
because of that... Th-The... You know—

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:42.980
Hey you!

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.780
What are you doing,
prattling on and on like that?

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.780
I'm sorry!

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:49.280
Enough with the idle chatter!
Get to work!

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:50.490
Right.

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.830
I'm so sorry.
It's my fault for talking so much.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:56.330
Um...

00:05:56.790 --> 00:06:00.250
Please be careful when you pass by the ureter.

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.710
The ureter?

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.050
Oh boy! Talk about refreshing!

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.510
Wanna go again
after we're done with this round?

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:13.310
I don't think we should rely
on the Glomeruli too much.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:15.680
You saw how they were working
so hard in silence.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:19.190
You're no fun! What a straight arrow!

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:24.530
Do you hear that weird sound?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.530
Huh?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.320
This is near the ureter, right?

00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:31.990
Isn't this where the urine
that the kidneys just produced comes through?

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.700
No. It sounds like something's stuck.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:41.080
<i>Please be careful when you pass by the ureter.</i>

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:45.880
The wall!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.720
Wh-What the cell are those?

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:57.520
The ureter's been ruptured!

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.890
The foreign object is still lodged inside!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:01.600
Not looking good for spontaneous passage!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.360
A one-centimeter stone?

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:06.780
How are we supposed to deal with that?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.860
<i>Kidney stones.</i>

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:14.120
<i>The most common types of kidney stones
are calcium oxalate stones,</i>

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:20.710
<i>formed when the oxalic acid and calcium in the
waste filtered by kidneys crystalize in the urine.</i>

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:24.630
<i>Stones that are larger than one centimeter
are harder to pass naturally.</i>

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.470
The tear in the ureter is spreading!

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.930
Everybody, run! Please run!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:39.560
It's going to start bleeding!

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.400
<i>Gross hematuria.</i>

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.440
<i>When massive amounts
of Red Blood Cells enter the urine</i>

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.990
<i>until it can be perceived as red
by the naked eye.</i>

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.030
<i>When it's negligible and doesn't appear red
to the naked eye,</i>

00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:00.410
<i>it's called "microscopic hematuria"
or "uric blood."</i>

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.870
This is messed up!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.040
If we don't get out of here,
we'll end up getting swept away, too!

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.290
Acute pain has been triggered!

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.630
Both the heart rate
and blood pressure are rising!

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.470
<i>Kidney stones are sometimes accompanied
by pain so severe,</i>

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.350
<i>they're known as the "King of Pain."</i>

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.890
The kidney's internal pressure is rising!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.060
It's now affecting the cellular structure!

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.110
Gran—

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.360
Not another word out of you!

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.570
Listen to me. These kidneys
are known as "silent organs."

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.570
Whatever happens,
whining has no place here!

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:39.410
We've got to go on working in silence!

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:45.170
<i>Even if the kidneys start to malfunction,
symptoms are often hard to detect.</i>

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.380
<i>Hence they're known as "silent organs."</i>

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:57.300
Are you all right?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.050
Yeah.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.610
It stopped.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.360
Hey, what are you doing?

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:16.950
If it stays stuck in here,
the pain's only going to spread!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:22.370
We have to get rid of this,
for the Glomeruli's sake, too!

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.960
Huh? If that thing starts moving,

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.000
it could rip through the ureter again,
and then, we'd end up in the urine!

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:34.220
There it is again. You're so predictable.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:41.390
Ah, all right.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:45.520
- Wh-What's this?
- What's going on?

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.730
Something just entered via the urethra!

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:48.940
What?

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:56.110
URINE

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:56.110
And now, it's blowing past the bladder, wrenching
open the check valve and entering the ureter!

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.570
It's reached the kidney stone!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:11.340
What's this? What's this sound?
Is it coming from inside the ureter?

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.010
Wh-What the cell?

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.930
<i>Transurethral ureteroscopic lithotripsy.</i>

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:27.770
<i>A surgical method for smashing kidney stones with
lasers by inserting an endoscope into the urethra.</i>

00:10:27.770 --> 00:10:29.480
It's all crushed up.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.860
Th-The fragments of the stone
are flowing away!

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:37.610
- Are you all right?
- Hey...

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:40.700
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.700
White Blood Cell! So, you came to help?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:44.410
You couldn't look more thrilled, rookie.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:47.250
And we're not even on your radar!

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.250
Oh, hey, no, I didn't mean to...

00:10:50.540 --> 00:10:54.550
There's no time for idle chatter.
We're taking you to a place that escaped damage.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.500
Okay!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:58.840
Platelets, we're leaving the rest to you!

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.050
Sure thing! Let us handle this!

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:01.050
PLATELETS

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.890
There won't be any more stones
coming this way, right?

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.810
Like a really huge one?

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:08.930
If something like that happened,
we'd end up in the urine, too.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:11.650
Who cares?
If it happens, it happens!

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:14.570
Just get to work so that it doesn't happen!

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:16.320
Okay.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.400
The Platelets are having a tough time, too.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.330
White Blood Cell,
are you good to work now?

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:28.790
I think I'm in even better shape than before.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.250
Really?

00:11:30.750 --> 00:11:33.830
Well, that thing that was stuck in the ureter
got smashed up and washed away,

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:35.090
so I guess it's all good now.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.800
But it's still too early to relax.

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:39.840
Huh?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.260
That's right.

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:45.100
If we White Blood Cells
are gathered in one spot...

00:11:46.350 --> 00:11:48.850
That means that something's been detected.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:59.440
If we make our way back
through this tube,

00:11:59.440 --> 00:12:02.990
we can go all the way in!

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.240
Germs are heading this way
through the urethra?

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:10.620
Yes. They're using the tube that was inserted
into this body to make their way in.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:14.580
Meaning that they're on their way
to where the Glomeruli are.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.170
The kidneys.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:21.630
The bacteria has invaded
the bladder via the tube!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.840
How can this be happening?

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:27.260
Normally, the check valve
would protect it,

00:12:27.260 --> 00:12:31.810
making it hard for external bacteria
to reenter from the urethra.

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:37.900
Yes, but right now the tube that smashed
that kidney stone is inserted into the ureter,

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.530
so the bacteria can use it
to infiltrate all the way in.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.950
Is such a thing even possible?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.070
To our knowledge, it would only happen
in extremely rare cases.

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:50.410
So, this body's been abandoned
by luck, even?

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:56.170
At this time, the bacteria have reached
the bladder. If they breach the ureter...

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:59.380
it could cause acute pyelonephritis!

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:02.420
<i>Acute pyelonephritis.</i>

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:05.890
<i>An infection of the renal pelvis
where the kidneys store urine,</i>

00:13:05.890 --> 00:13:10.680
<i>triggered by a backflow of bacteria
from the urine.</i>

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:13.100
<i>Unless treated properly,</i>

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:17.400
<i>the bacteria can invade
the bloodstream or even cause sepsis.</i>

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:21.190
If the germs climb all the way up here...

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:26.200
They're here.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:27.360
Huh?

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.490
Whoa! Are you kidding me?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.750
You two get away from here.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.330
Let's go.

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.050
Everyone, attack mode.

00:13:44.920 --> 00:13:47.220
We can't let them get past us!

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.300
Whatever it takes, annihilate them!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:52.260
Charge!

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.940
Hey, where are you going?

00:13:57.940 --> 00:13:58.900
To the kidney!

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.520
Huh? Why would you go there?

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:05.070
Those germs are heading toward the kidney!
Didn't you hear White Blood Cell—

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:05.860
That's why we're going!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.490
Hey, are you serious?

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:11.490
Hey! Wait up, will you!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.000
Hey, you're on a roll!

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:21.840
Well, I haven't fought in a while,
so I'm bursting with all this extra energy.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.210
Still...

00:14:23.550 --> 00:14:26.090
talk about outnumbered!

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:29.930
Well, we did get decimated
in that gonococci battle.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.930
The White Blood Cells are struggling!

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.600
At this rate, it's only a matter of time
before the kidney's breached!

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:37.600
Did you call on the Macrophages for backup?

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.810
I did. However...

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:43.520
it will be a while before they get there.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.400
<i>Macrophages.</i>

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.490
<i>They advance at a slower speed
than White Blood Cells.</i>

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.450
If worst comes to worst,
we'll have to abandon the kidney.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:54.700
What?

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:56.790
The body has two kidneys.

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.750
Even if one is lost...

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.210
the body can still survive.

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:02.710
If that were to happen...

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.170
what would become of the Glomeruli
who work in the abandoned kidney?

00:15:06.760 --> 00:15:09.050
I said it was the worst case scenario!

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:14.010
Hang in there to ensure
it doesn't end up that way, White Blood Cells!

00:15:24.190 --> 00:15:25.520
<i>Pyuria.</i>

00:15:25.520 --> 00:15:29.740
<i>When bacteria invades the urinary tract,
triggering inflammation,</i>

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:34.490
<i>leading to White Blood Cells permeating the urine
which gives it a cloudy appearance.</i>

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:38.410
We don't have
enough White Blood Cells as it is!

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.370
Everybody!

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.580
The germs are closing in!

00:15:43.830 --> 00:15:44.790
Hide!

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:48.260
Not happening! Get back to work!

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:50.090
Gran...

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:53.340
It's an emergency!
This is no time to be talking like—

00:15:53.340 --> 00:15:55.800
This is a silent organ.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:59.100
We've got to go on working in silence
no matter what!

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:04.520
Please...

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.400
don't push them any harder
than you already are.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:09.900
Just let them...

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:13.910
Just let them complain a little now and then!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.240
Listen to what they have to say!

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.620
You're really overstepping.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:22.290
What?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:25.750
We have our own way of doing things.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:27.500
I'll thank you not to butt in!

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:32.260
She's right.
This has nothing to do with us.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.510
Come on, let's go.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.470
I-If I may, Gran...

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:45.060
It's true that you're strict, Gran,
but you taught us everything about our work,

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:47.770
so we're all very grateful to you.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:53.150
And we do understand
that you're strict with us because you care.

00:16:54.450 --> 00:16:58.410
So, we have no intention
of complaining or whining.

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.790
Even so...

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.000
Even so...

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.080
there are times
when we want to just cry!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:13.720
The germs got this far?

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:21.470
Look out!

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:29.980
Gran?

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:41.910
White Blood Cell!

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:50.250
I couldn't hold them back in the ureter.

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:53.880
But I won't let them
get any farther than this.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.800
Gran! Gran!

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:04.100
Gran, I'm so sorry.
If it wasn't... If it wasn't for me...

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.600
Are you okay?

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.770
But why?

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:14.240
Forgive me for always giving you all
such a hard time.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:18.110
At least, I got to make up for it
in the end. Thank goodness.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.030
Don't talk like this is the end! Gran!

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:25.040
I want you to keep on teaching us
all about the kidneys!

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.210
Gran!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:33.920
Wh-What is it, Gran?

00:18:35.670 --> 00:18:37.380
Get to work.

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.310
You're still Kidney Cells.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:47.560
It's up to the rest of you
who are left to get it done.

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:53.570
<i>Humans are born
with approximately two million Glomeruli...</i>

00:18:53.570 --> 00:18:58.570
<i>but these numbers gradually dwindle, as once
damaged, the Glomeruli can't regenerate.</i>

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:06.660
Unless we keep working, this body
will soon be riddled with waste products.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:10.670
We're a silent organ.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.710
Get to work... in silence.

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:19.010
You have to... work.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:34.190
Thank you!

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:36.610
Still...

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:37.360
Yeah.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:41.450
No matter how many of them we slash,
more and more keep popping up!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.450
What's that?

00:19:47.120 --> 00:19:50.410
<i>Target identified. Now disinfecting.</i>

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.420
<i>New quinolone antibacterial drug.</i>

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:03.720
<i>Drugs that act as bactericides
by inhibiting DNA gyrase activity.</i>

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:10.480
<i>Effective against urinary, intestinal
and respiratory infections.</i>

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:13.350
The antibiotics have arrived!

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.940
Looks like the cells will be able to hold on!

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.530
Is that right?

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:27.490
<i>If we keep barely coming out on top
in these battles, one of these days...</i>

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:35.920
Come this way, please.

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:36.670
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:20:37.420 --> 00:20:40.880
Please wash off all those
waste products and freshen up.

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:48.140
We're going to go all around the body now.

00:20:48.140 --> 00:20:51.270
But look how soiled you are.
You shouldn't.

00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:53.600
We'll be totally fine
for just one round, right?

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:54.400
Huh?

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.730
- Let's go.
- Uh, yeah, I guess.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:04.030
Even if it's just for a split second,

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.070
go ahead and cry your eyes out.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:08.330
For your Gran's sake, too.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:12.040
Huh! Acting so cool...

00:21:12.040 --> 00:21:13.750
That's not what that was about.

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:18.170
<i>Once again, it really hit home.</i>

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:23.470
<i>That even if you're suffering,</i>

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:25.510
<i>and let yourself complain about it,</i>

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.550
<i>there's nothing you can do.</i>

00:21:27.970 --> 00:21:31.270
<i>That's what a code black environment is.</i>

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.980
<i>Even so...</i>

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:35.850
<i>I...</i>

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:42.230
I'm feeling that power surge!

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:46.240
Awesome! Who knew that there was
still a heaven in this world?

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.910
This totally rocks!

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.500
PREVIEW

00:23:20.920 --> 00:23:24.420
Here it comes!
I can feel it surging!

00:23:22.710 --> 00:23:24.040
CAFFEINE

00:23:24.420 --> 00:23:26.760
This is manna from heaven.

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:26.760
TEMPTATION

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:28.630
Even if I'm right next to him...

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:30.050
JEALOUSY

00:23:29.260 --> 00:23:33.350
all I ever do is try to run away.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:34.010
CAFFEINE, TEMPTATION, AND JEALOUSY
